{% extends '_article.jinja' %}
{% from 'data/pages.jinja' import catalogue %}
{% set article = catalogue['roadmap'] %}
{% set implemented = [
  'Worker-backed stream, file, rotation, socket, and HTTP output.',
  'Named logger hierarchy, restricted configuration, and callback filtering.',
  'Inline structured fields and scoped context through named loggers.',
  'Rust log/tracing bridges behind optional features.',
] %}
{% set planned = [
  ('Formatter registration', 'Named formatter identifiers that resolve to working formatters, not exported placeholders.'),
  ('Batching', 'Handler-side batches that amortize transport cost without hiding drops or reordering.'),
  ('Benchmark reporting', 'Published results backed by runnable artefacts and workload metadata.'),
  ('Observability exporters', 'Journald and OpenTelemetry sinks, configured explicitly. The tracing bridge is a separate capability.'),
] %}
{% set whatifs = [
  ('petri-context', 'Context that follows the task', 'A contextvars-backed scope could keep fields isolated across awaits. It needs cancellation, nesting, and bridge-boundary tests before replacing thread-local context.'),
  ('petri-batch', 'Batches with an accountable boundary', 'A batch-aware handler could amortize transport cost. Ordering, partial failure, flush barriers, and overflow accounting must remain explicit.'),
  ('petri-gauge', 'A closer instrument view', 'A future inspection surface could expose queue pressure without inventing durability guarantees. Any visualization must report observed counters and their scope.'),
] %}
{% block article_body %}
<section aria-labelledby="implemented"><h2 id="implemented">Implemented in the documented source</h2>
<p class="fl-status fl-status--done">{{ ui.icon('check') }} Implemented · Release forthcoming</p>
<ul class="fl-checklist">{% for item in implemented %}<li>{{ ui.icon('check') }}<span>{{ item }}</span></li>{% endfor %}</ul>
<p>The next assumed release is {{ femto_version }}. These statements describe revision <code>{{ femto_revision[:7] }}</code>, not an already published beta.</p>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="planned"><h2 id="planned">Planned work</h2>
<p class="fl-status">{{ ui.icon('info') }} Planned · No delivery date</p>
<ul class="fl-checklist fl-checklist--open">{% for title, text in planned %}<li><span class="fl-checklist__box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><strong>{{ title }}.</strong> {{ text }}</span></li>{% endfor %}</ul>
<p><a href="{{ source_base }}/docs/roadmap.md">Read the upstream roadmap at the documented revision.</a> Check <a href="{{ repository_url }}/blob/main/docs/roadmap.md">the live roadmap</a> for subsequent progress.</p>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="exploratory"><h2 id="exploratory">What-ifs from the field station</h2>
<p class="fl-status fl-status--explore">{{ ui.icon('microscope') }} Exploratory · Ideas in the petri dish</p>
<p>The cultures below are design questions, not commitments. Each names what would have to be proven before it could become planned work.</p>
<div class="fl-whatifs">{% for key, title, text in whatifs %}<article class="fl-whatif">{{ ui.plate(key, 'whatif', sizes='(width < 768px) 100vw, 240px') }}<div><p class="fl-label">Exploratory · Culture {{ '%02d' | format(loop.index) }}</p><h3>{{ title }}</h3><p>{{ text }}</p></div></article>{% endfor %}</div>
<p>The concepts suggest alternative futures. They do not set release promises.</p>
</section>
{% endblock %}
